@@ -0,0 +1,5 @@
+Reconstructing consolidated metadata no longer depends on the order in which the
+flat keys were persisted. Previously, children of sibling nodes whose names sort
+equally (for example, names differing only by case) could interleave, so some
+nodes were dropped from their parent's consolidated metadata and remained as
+unreachable slash-containing keys at the top level.
